      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Denmark has ratified a security deal with the US and Greenland, DW reports.",
      "cites": [
        "news:dw:97c7c7d282a7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:09Z",
      "text": "France 24, Al Jazeera and The Guardian also reported the story.",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:274d8e9dcbf1",
        "news:aljazeera:7cedea4ee0b7",
        "news:guardian:f9c1853256b3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:18Z",
      "text": "World Bank figures show Greenland's GDP growth was 0.6% in 2018, 2.8% in 2019 and 0.3% in 2020.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG:GL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:20Z",
      "text": "It then rose to 1.6% in 2021, 2.0% in 2022 and 0.9% in 2023.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG:GL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:24Z",
      "text": "Greenland is an autonomous territory of the Kingdom of Denmark.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386489605:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:29Z",
      "text": "By land area, it is the largest of the kingdom's three constituent parts, alongside Denmark proper and the Faroe Islands.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386489605:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:35Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined it: “Denmark ratifies Greenland security deal after months of pressure by Trump”.",
